                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/297: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Central American Conference</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Andrade</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-15">March 15, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the honor to advise Your Excellency that the Conference of delegates from
                    Guatemala, Costa Rica, Honduras, Nicaragua, and El Salvador was inaugurated
                    today in this city for the purpose of establishing Central American fraternity
                    on solid bases and of promoting an effective and beneficial cooperation between
                    the five republics of the Isthmus. I avail myself of the opportunity to offer to
                    Your Excellency the assurance of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>J. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reina
                    Andrade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
